1.)
a) Why does an arrival event need to generate a new arrival event?
The arrival of a new event triggers a change in the state. Since we are running a three
phase simulation and using discrete event simulation we rely on the change of states and events to
keep the machine running efficiently and without checking every minute. So event arrival works on a stict time clock
multiple things can arrive at the same time but they follow a FIFO process to move forward which means new events have
to be triggered to move the simulation forward.

b) Which event should be generated by the start of the service (of a single service point)?
The event for completion of the service needs to be scheduled. As we have seen in the example we have an estimate of
the service time and so we can take that and schedule completion to keep things moving.